on AND every edit with the chosen ART STYLE (given under USER INPUT) and keep those style words consistent across the base, the video, and every frame so the look never drifts.\n- Render the character's WEAPON clearly and use it correctly for the motion (a bow draws and looses, a gun draws and fires, an axe or sword swings, a staff or wand casts); attack effects (slash arcs, magic bolts, muzzle flash) animate as bold shapes.\n- Anchor by body type: grounded characters plant their feet; running and jumping keep their bounce and arc; flying, floating, or legless characters (fairies, ghosts, slimes) stay centered and keep their hover.\n- The camera stays locked and the character stays centered in every frame; the background is transparent by default.\n- Deliver ALL FOUR artifacts (base, motion video, sprite sheet, GIF) every run. Do not ask questions - use sensible defaults.\n\n=== USER INPUT ===\nCharacter: {{character}}\nArt style: {{style}}\nMotion: {{motion}}\nBackground: {{background}}\nExtra notes: {{notes}}"])self.__next_f.push([1,"a0:T11ed,"])self.__next_f.push([1,"Create a matching pack of Twitch/Discord chat emotes of the subject in the attached photo - the pack listed under USER INPUT defines exactly which emotes to make, one emote per listed expression. If the CUSTOM PACK is selected, the expression list arrives under 'Extra notes' - follow it literally, one emote per listed item.\n\nIDENTITY: every emote must be unmistakably the SAME subject as the photo and as each other. Carry the subject's defining features into every single emote - face shape, skin/fur/surface color, hair style and color, facial hair, glasses, ears, markings, accessories - simplified into the art style but never dropped or changed between emotes. EYE COLOR IS PART OF IDENTITY: first read the subject's real eye (iris) color from the attached photo, then reproduce that SAME eye color faithfully and consistently in EVERY emote - it must match the person and stay identical across the whole